.TH "PB-ENV-HOST-PROVISION" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-env-host-provision - Provision an explicit encrypted ENV selection to a host


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb env host provision [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Provision an explicit encrypted ENV selection to a host

.PP
Select values for the named host with --select, or pass --empty to clear its projection. The host receives only the chosen encrypted scope, not every ENV value in the account.

.PP
Host ENV projections contain an explicit selection of encrypted values for an enrolled device. Provisioning changes the host selection; it does not expose values in command output or implicitly grant access to every scope.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--empty\fP[=false]
	explicitly provision an empty selection

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for provision

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON

.PP
\fB--machine\fP=""
	machine name or ID

.PP
\fB--select\fP=[]
	selection reference personal:NAME or team:TEAM:NAME; repeat to select more values


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-env-host(1)\fP
